SN PFile Support Update
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
-----  UPDATE 01/07/96  -----

Well, nothing has changed from last update except I'm switching over a bit
earlier than planned.  Until further notice, please send all mail to the
standby account, beazleyp@mqg-smtp3.usmc.mil...

-----  UPDATE 12/15/95  -----

This is a bad time for Internet access for me...  In about six weeks, I'll
be leaving Cuba (around the last part of January) and returning to Camp
Lejeune, NC.  I'm currently going through a divorce, also, which should be
finalized in mid-February (yes!), so I won't be living at home, obviously.
I'm going to be stuck in barracks until the end of my term in the USMC,
currently February 7th, 1997 but subject to change depending on the outcome
of my request for early release for education.  If that happens, I should
be out no later than December 15th, 1996, and I'll be returning to Odessa,
TX.

Anyway, living in the barracks, I won't have a phone of my own, therefore,
my BBS will NOT be going back online as previously planned and I will not
have direct access to the Internet anymore.  So my two primary means of
support will not be available.

I am terminating my Holonet account (beazley@holonet.net) on or around the
20th of January.  After that, I can be reached at my old standby account
at work, beazleyp@mqg-smtp3.usmc.mil...  If there are any changes in that,
I'll let it be known somehow.

Sorry for the confusing times, but it can't be helped, unfortunately.

Midnight (Phil Beazley)      Hard-core Amiga user & SysOp since 1986!
beazley@holonet.net             Amiga 1200/030/28, 10M/370M HD, 28.8k
                           Finger me for my GeekCode & PGP Public Key!

-----  UPDATE 11/24/95  -----

My Internet address has changed!  I will still receive mail at the above
address, but the frequency of checking that box will be MUCH less often
than my new account...  My new address is below.

Also, I'm including PGP signatures of the main file(s) and my public key
with my newer releases.  If you don't trust the key included, please
don't hesitate to request one from me via e-mail or by finger.

If there's not a .sig for the main program file, STOP.  Delete the archive
and get it somewhere else.  Who knows what someone has done to it.  If
you can't find anywhere else, I will take requests via e-mail.

-----  UPDATE 09/18/95  -----

During the period from August 18th to February 18th (latter date subject to
change), direct support from me will only be available via the Internet.

I'm currently down in Guantanamo Bay, Cuba, and only have Internet e-mail
access.  I'll be getting my PFiles out one way or another, most likely
through someone who can upload these files to Aminet.  Also, I'm attempting
to get my files back to Amiga Underground (as stated in the docs/guides
accompanying my PFiles), so there's a chance they can be received there.

My Internet address is beazleyp@mqg-smtp3.usmc.mil and I'll be checking
very frequently.  (I don't have much else to do here.)  Please send any
comments/suggestions/bug reports to that address and I'll get back to you
that day...

Thanks and can't wait to get back to the states, but while I'm here, I'm
taking full advantage of the time and coding my brains out.  See ya'...
